1
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:37,527
This is a time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,807 --> 00:02:41,827
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:42,047 --> 00:02:46,007
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:46,587 --> 00:02:50,887
Maki D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum-gum fruit,

5
00:02:51,167 --> 00:02:53,647
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:54,027 --> 00:02:56,607
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,607 --> 00:02:59,747
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,747 --> 00:03:02,847
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:04,167 --> 00:03:05,547
This is a sight!

10
00:03:06,587 --> 00:03:09,387
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:10,047 --> 00:03:13,167
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:13,387 --> 00:03:17,447
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:21,127 --> 00:03:23,687
In an attempt to rescue his brother Ace,

14
00:03:23,687 --> 00:03:27,027
Luffy enlisted the aid of the pirate empress, Boa Hancock,

15
00:03:27,027 --> 00:03:30,447
to sneak onto a Navy vessel bound for Impel Down.

16
00:03:30,907 --> 00:03:33,567
I'm sure you heard about what your brother's been up to.

17
00:03:34,287 --> 00:03:36,667
Now, I don't expect us to get along perfect,

18
00:03:37,167 --> 00:03:41,847
but challenging the world government head-on and wrecking up Eni's lobby is over the line.

19
00:03:41,847 --> 00:03:47,727
Oh, by the way, I told the little punk about his father.

20
00:03:49,727 --> 00:03:51,907
Of course, the news took him by surprise.

21
00:03:52,567 --> 00:03:53,607
Can't blame the boy.

22
00:03:53,607 --> 00:03:56,327
Our fathers.

23
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:58,147
To hell with them.

24
00:03:58,687 --> 00:04:01,287
And to hell with you if you ever thought we could be Marines.

25
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:05,047
We've both got the blood of criminals flowing through our veins.

26
00:04:05,767 --> 00:04:09,047
And that was the only gift those bastards ever gave us.

27
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:13,447
I took the name Portgus from my mother because I owe her so much.

28
00:04:13,447 --> 00:04:17,007
But I don't owe my father a damned thing.

29
00:04:17,787 --> 00:04:19,447
I don't even remember the bastard.

30
00:04:20,547 --> 00:04:22,267
He can keep his name.

31
00:04:23,187 --> 00:04:24,447
I know, I know.

32
00:04:24,667 --> 00:04:25,827
But the man tried.

33
00:04:25,967 --> 00:04:26,587
He wanted to...

34
00:04:26,587 --> 00:04:27,667
Enough, all right!

35
00:04:29,867 --> 00:04:31,027
Listen to me.

36
00:04:32,787 --> 00:04:33,827
Don't fight it.

37
00:04:34,087 --> 00:04:34,727
Run wild.

38
00:04:35,007 --> 00:04:37,807
With us, our flag will be yours.

39
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:40,467
And I will call you my son.

40
00:04:41,267 --> 00:04:42,927
Whitebeard is my only father.

41
00:04:42,927 --> 00:04:47,667
Got it, old man.

42
00:04:50,747 --> 00:04:52,967
Better for us to quit while we're still ahead.

43
00:04:54,207 --> 00:04:55,667
Bucky the Clown had a good run.

44
00:04:55,787 --> 00:04:58,127
But I'm afraid his luck as a pirate has run out.

45
00:04:58,287 --> 00:04:58,627
No!

46
00:04:58,927 --> 00:05:00,287
I refuse to accept it.

47
00:05:00,507 --> 00:05:01,667
He's a man among men.

48
00:05:01,867 --> 00:05:04,787
The only way Captain Buggy can go out is in a blaze of glory.

49
00:05:05,667 --> 00:05:06,467
All right.

50
00:05:06,987 --> 00:05:07,787
Impel down.

51
00:05:08,207 --> 00:05:08,987
This is it.

52
00:05:08,987 --> 00:05:14,027
Welcome to my prison.

53
00:05:14,407 --> 00:05:15,367
Impel down.

54
00:05:16,267 --> 00:05:17,707
Oops, jumped the gun there.

55
00:05:18,007 --> 00:05:20,787
It's not, well, exactly mine just yet.

56
00:05:21,027 --> 00:05:23,007
I'm the Vice Warden here, Hannibal.

57
00:05:23,227 --> 00:05:24,367
Well, for now at least.

58
00:05:24,767 --> 00:05:26,427
It's a pleasure to meet you, Vice Admiral.

59
00:05:26,427 --> 00:05:29,447
Oh, and don't forget these.

60
00:05:30,187 --> 00:05:32,227
Keep in mind that they're sea prism stone.

61
00:05:32,847 --> 00:05:35,407
You call me a visitor here, not a prisoner.

62
00:05:35,987 --> 00:05:37,527
Then you put me in those?

63
00:05:37,527 --> 00:05:44,807
Countdown to Ace's execution.

64
00:05:45,707 --> 00:05:47,847
Thirty-three hours.

65
00:05:52,167 --> 00:05:53,787
A reunion in hell?

66
00:05:54,087 --> 00:05:56,067
The man who ate the chop-chop fruit.

67
00:05:56,067 --> 00:06:09,847
You'd leave me powerless?

68
00:06:10,507 --> 00:06:11,427
How cruel.

69
00:06:14,107 --> 00:06:15,307
But necessary.

70
00:06:15,307 --> 00:06:45,287
The man who ate the chop-chop fruit.

71
00:06:45,307 --> 00:06:47,507
Be gentle, I'm delicate.

72
00:06:50,507 --> 00:06:52,767
What happened?

73
00:06:57,647 --> 00:06:59,107
It's safe now, Luffy.

74
00:07:02,107 --> 00:07:03,907
Wow, that was close.

75
00:07:04,567 --> 00:07:08,967
I was starting to think I'd just have to crawl out from there like a cockroach and hope for the best.

76
00:07:08,967 --> 00:07:11,887
That power of yours is really handy in a pinch, huh?

77
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:16,167
Even so, I'm afraid that this is as far as I'll be able to accompany you.

78
00:07:16,667 --> 00:07:20,087
They're quite insistent on placing me in those sea prism stone handcuffs.

79
00:07:20,347 --> 00:07:22,747
And once they take my cloak, you'll have nowhere to hide.

80
00:07:23,847 --> 00:07:27,307
I just wish... I wish I could do more to help you, but...

81
00:07:27,307 --> 00:07:28,627
Aw, don't talk like that.

82
00:07:28,887 --> 00:07:30,547
You got me in this place, didn't you?

83
00:07:30,587 --> 00:07:32,147
That's more than I could have done alone.

84
00:07:32,147 --> 00:07:35,667
Even though there's guards everywhere, we made it all this way, no problem.

85
00:07:36,027 --> 00:07:37,207
I can handle the rest.

86
00:07:38,747 --> 00:07:39,147
Luffy.

87
00:07:42,347 --> 00:07:46,387
Breaking your brother out will be challenging enough, but if you get captured as well,

88
00:07:46,787 --> 00:07:48,607
who knows what horrors you might face.

89
00:07:49,007 --> 00:07:52,027
One wrong step and you may never see the light of day again.

90
00:07:52,027 --> 00:07:57,467
I know you want to save Ace, but this is dangerous.

91
00:07:58,447 --> 00:08:00,527
Please, take care of yourself, too.

92
00:08:02,527 --> 00:08:04,767
I won't let you down, you have my word.

93
00:08:04,967 --> 00:08:07,127
Thanks for everything, Hancock, you're the best.

94
00:08:08,187 --> 00:08:11,807
I won't forget what you've done, not for the rest of my life.

95
00:08:11,807 --> 00:08:14,507
He just called me by my name.

96
00:08:15,167 --> 00:08:17,447
My real, actual name.

97
00:08:17,907 --> 00:08:19,127
For the first time.

98
00:08:19,127 --> 00:08:23,047
Cool, whatever works for you, Hammock.

99
00:08:23,227 --> 00:08:25,127
Can I get seconds over here, Hammock?

100
00:08:25,387 --> 00:08:26,907
Hey, Hammock, what are you doing?

101
00:08:30,947 --> 00:08:32,267
Hey, Hancock.

102
00:08:41,267 --> 00:08:43,447
My life is finally complete.

103
00:08:43,687 --> 00:08:44,847
I can die happy.

104
00:08:44,847 --> 00:08:50,047
Hey, you can turn that lady back now.

105
00:08:50,107 --> 00:08:51,287
I should be fine up here.

106
00:08:52,307 --> 00:08:53,047
Say it, Luffy.

107
00:08:53,647 --> 00:08:54,607
Say my name again.

108
00:08:55,647 --> 00:08:56,287
Uh, what?

109
00:08:56,947 --> 00:08:58,547
This is taking too long.

110
00:08:58,787 --> 00:09:00,487
This situation is unprecedented.

111
00:09:00,767 --> 00:09:02,467
She's probably just being thorough.

112
00:09:02,467 --> 00:09:02,807
Huh.

113
00:09:04,187 --> 00:09:04,547
Heh.

114
00:09:04,767 --> 00:09:06,747
A thorough body search.

115
00:09:07,087 --> 00:09:07,187
Hm.

116
00:09:07,727 --> 00:09:08,307
Ah!

117
00:09:09,247 --> 00:09:11,667
Oh, that's so naughty!

118
00:09:11,667 --> 00:09:15,127
Get your mind out of the gutter, damn it!

119
00:09:17,127 --> 00:09:22,287
Uh, Vice Warden Hannibal, we're not getting any visuals from the surveillance nail in the examination room.

120
00:09:22,407 --> 00:09:24,407
Is there something going on in there we don't know about?

121
00:09:24,687 --> 00:09:25,027
Huh?

122
00:09:26,787 --> 00:09:28,447
Domino, something wrong in there?

123
00:09:30,187 --> 00:09:31,427
No answer, huh?

124
00:09:32,307 --> 00:09:33,107
It's okay.

125
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:34,627
I'm the Vice Warden, right?

126
00:09:34,867 --> 00:09:37,147
Checking things out in there is strictly business, you see?

127
00:09:37,147 --> 00:09:41,087
Even if that business happens to involve two hot chicks touching each other!

128
00:09:41,767 --> 00:09:42,047
Ugh.

129
00:09:44,687 --> 00:09:45,167
Huh?

130
00:09:45,667 --> 00:09:46,067
Hm.

131
00:09:48,647 --> 00:09:50,927
We have completed the body search, sir.

132
00:09:51,227 --> 00:09:51,627
Ugh.

133
00:09:51,827 --> 00:09:52,787
Beep, beep.

134
00:09:53,447 --> 00:09:54,567
Scratch that last report.

135
00:09:54,847 --> 00:09:55,787
Everything is fine here.

136
00:09:55,947 --> 00:09:57,507
I hope I didn't cause a problem, sir.

137
00:09:57,807 --> 00:09:59,167
Did the exam take too long?

138
00:09:59,527 --> 00:09:59,867
Huh?

139
00:10:00,387 --> 00:10:00,787
No.

140
00:10:01,427 --> 00:10:02,907
Everything's fine on our end, too.

141
00:10:02,907 --> 00:10:07,607
I see that your guests are treated as poorly as your prisoners here.

142
00:10:07,887 --> 00:10:09,967
Surely an Empress deserves better than this.

143
00:10:10,267 --> 00:10:11,047
It is a pity.

144
00:10:11,447 --> 00:10:14,767
But in Impel Down, we can't afford to make exceptions to the rules.

145
00:10:15,387 --> 00:10:18,367
I wonder why I can't shake this strange feeling.

146
00:10:19,187 --> 00:10:20,047
Lead the way.

147
00:10:20,547 --> 00:10:21,167
Ah, yes.

148
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:22,747
If you'll let me in front, please.

149
00:10:23,187 --> 00:10:24,667
Or just go that way.

150
00:10:24,667 --> 00:10:33,587
Before we visit Ace, we'll take this elevator to what we call the Burning Heat Floor,

151
00:10:33,687 --> 00:10:36,027
where we'll stop by the Warden Magellan's office.

152
00:10:36,427 --> 00:10:39,027
Fair warning, as the name implies, it's quite hot there.

153
00:10:45,387 --> 00:10:45,827
Luffy.

154
00:10:47,947 --> 00:10:49,767
Be bold, but be safe.

155
00:10:51,947 --> 00:10:52,847
Bye, Encom.

156
00:10:52,987 --> 00:10:53,767
Thank you.

157
00:10:53,767 --> 00:10:56,887
Is something wrong?

158
00:11:04,187 --> 00:11:08,347
Hancock, I love you.

159
00:11:09,487 --> 00:11:11,867
Oh, he really does love me.

160
00:11:13,907 --> 00:11:15,307
He's Empress Hancock.

161
00:11:15,387 --> 00:11:15,987
What's wrong?

162
00:11:16,207 --> 00:11:17,187
Do you need mouth to mouth?

163
00:11:17,207 --> 00:11:17,847
Are you ill?

164
00:11:18,187 --> 00:11:20,047
You were fine just a moment ago.

165
00:11:20,167 --> 00:11:20,667
What happened?

166
00:11:23,767 --> 00:11:34,247
Okay, not sure where to take things from here.

167
00:11:34,787 --> 00:11:37,027
Hancock said Ace is probably underwater.

168
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:39,887
Looks like that elevator might head down a long way.

169
00:11:41,047 --> 00:11:41,867
Oh, yeah.

170
00:11:42,247 --> 00:11:44,227
The fever cart might come in handy.

171
00:11:44,227 --> 00:12:13,707
Looks like they grabbed dinner, too.

172
00:12:13,707 --> 00:12:14,827
Open the hatch.

173
00:12:19,207 --> 00:12:20,087
Nice work.

174
00:12:20,667 --> 00:12:22,347
Get it to the fridge and we'll be done.

175
00:12:22,347 --> 00:12:30,927
Hope you're feeling better, Empress.

176
00:12:31,107 --> 00:12:33,527
We should be passing through level one any second now.

177
00:12:33,527 --> 00:12:42,287
Let me out of here, dammit!

178
00:12:44,867 --> 00:12:46,807
It's even worse than I expected.

179
00:12:47,207 --> 00:12:48,127
Surely dust.

180
00:12:48,907 --> 00:12:53,387
This floor hosts relatively minor offenders, so these whippings are mostly a formality.

181
00:12:53,607 --> 00:12:54,067
Madness.

182
00:12:54,067 --> 00:12:55,607
Yes, and yet it's the truth.

183
00:12:56,607 --> 00:13:00,867
Level one of Impel Down is known as the Crimson Floor, by the way.

184
00:13:01,067 --> 00:13:02,487
What's crimson about it?

185
00:13:02,607 --> 00:13:03,647
That would be a secret.

186
00:13:04,827 --> 00:13:08,027
Level two is the floor of wild beasts from hell.

187
00:13:08,387 --> 00:13:09,207
Pretty straightforward.

188
00:13:09,207 --> 00:13:14,487
As we move deeper underwater, we reach level three, the starvation floor.

189
00:13:14,887 --> 00:13:19,187
Followed by level four, the burning heat floor, which is our destination.

190
00:13:20,127 --> 00:13:23,807
You can't tell from the surface, but this structure is actually quite expansive.

191
00:13:24,147 --> 00:13:28,167
Since it takes a while for this elevator to get to level four, you'll have plenty of time

192
00:13:28,167 --> 00:13:30,087
to indulge in the cacophony of screams.

193
00:13:30,387 --> 00:13:32,367
And is Fire Fist Ace on level four?

194
00:13:32,747 --> 00:13:34,967
No, and that isn't the bottom floor, either.

195
00:13:35,127 --> 00:13:37,087
We have a wide selection of torturous...

196
00:13:37,087 --> 00:13:37,447
Luffy.

197
00:13:41,527 --> 00:13:43,547
He should be down these stairs somewhere.

198
00:13:50,367 --> 00:13:52,107
No fair, you cheater!

199
00:13:52,147 --> 00:13:53,387
We thought you were just a clown.

200
00:13:53,527 --> 00:13:54,707
You didn't tell us you could do that?

201
00:13:54,867 --> 00:13:55,767
Can it, would you?

202
00:13:55,947 --> 00:13:57,927
The real clowns here are you losers.

203
00:13:58,167 --> 00:13:59,947
Getting whipped like dogs every damn day.

204
00:14:00,207 --> 00:14:02,487
Of course I'm going to break out the first chance I get.

205
00:14:02,647 --> 00:14:04,287
Are you just going to run out on us?

206
00:14:04,527 --> 00:14:04,927
Huh?

207
00:14:06,047 --> 00:14:09,347
That sounds like something a friend would say, and you folks are no friends of mine.

208
00:14:09,527 --> 00:14:11,987
I'm a free eagle chump, so deal with it.

209
00:14:12,107 --> 00:14:14,827
If you don't like being in there, why don't you slip out like me?

210
00:14:15,247 --> 00:14:16,407
What's that you can't?

211
00:14:16,587 --> 00:14:18,627
Well, I guess you're just going to have to die, huh?

212
00:14:20,327 --> 00:14:21,527
Kiss my ass, Thomas!

213
00:14:21,727 --> 00:14:22,147
Come on!

214
00:14:22,227 --> 00:14:23,427
You won't get away with this.

215
00:14:23,847 --> 00:14:24,127
Funky!

216
00:14:24,127 --> 00:14:29,807
I'm getting away just fine!

217
00:14:29,807 --> 00:14:42,587
A surveillance transponder snail?

218
00:14:42,587 --> 00:14:55,787
A surveillance transponder snail!

219
00:15:12,587 --> 00:15:15,127
Eeeeeeeeeuuuuuuuuuuuhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh

220
00:15:19,207 --> 00:15:20,787
Hi fellas.

221
00:15:20,787 --> 00:15:25,247
We found him! That's Buggy the Clown, prisoner from level 1, Community Cell Number 4.

222
00:15:25,247 --> 00:15:28,327
He's in the hallway in front of solitary cell number 22.

223
00:15:28,327 --> 00:15:29,647
Grab him and quit!

224
00:15:29,647 --> 00:15:34,087
Gah, damn it. Stupid snail! This is all your fault!

225
00:15:37,467 --> 00:15:40,747
The transponder snail 71 has been shut off!

226
00:15:40,747 --> 00:15:42,187
You blew it Buggy old pal.

227
00:15:42,187 --> 00:15:44,987
Don't come crying to us when they're torturing you to death.

228
00:15:45,187 --> 00:15:46,327
Serves you right, you dummy.

229
00:15:46,447 --> 00:15:48,467
Yeah, he'll wish he was dead for sure.

230
00:15:51,947 --> 00:15:53,507
Here come the Lugoni.

231
00:15:53,887 --> 00:15:54,807
Happy hunting.

232
00:15:55,267 --> 00:15:56,407
Make him suffer.

233
00:16:02,307 --> 00:16:05,467
The fever card keeps leading me down, but now what?

234
00:16:05,907 --> 00:16:07,087
Guess I'm out of stairs.

235
00:16:12,187 --> 00:16:14,807
All right, men. We're looking for prisoner 8,200.

236
00:16:14,947 --> 00:16:17,027
What? The stupid clown?

237
00:16:19,027 --> 00:16:22,027
No one knew he had devil fruit powers. You got the handcuffs?

238
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:23,027
Yeah, we're good.

239
00:16:24,527 --> 00:16:25,367
Let's move.

240
00:16:26,367 --> 00:16:27,787
Spread up and flank him.

241
00:16:31,547 --> 00:16:32,907
Cool. I made it.

242
00:16:33,007 --> 00:16:33,507
Hurry!

243
00:16:35,667 --> 00:16:36,787
Wonder what's up.

244
00:16:42,187 --> 00:16:44,887
So all of these are prison cells?

245
00:16:47,367 --> 00:16:48,527
What's that?

246
00:16:49,327 --> 00:16:50,827
I gotta get moving.

247
00:16:57,907 --> 00:17:01,187
Go away, you bunch of jerks!

248
00:17:05,507 --> 00:17:07,987
Have mercy on me!

249
00:17:07,987 --> 00:17:14,427
This way!

250
00:17:23,707 --> 00:17:24,407
Go on.

251
00:17:24,887 --> 00:17:26,087
Huh? Danger.

252
00:17:26,807 --> 00:17:29,447
It already has a skull. Who's gonna press it?

253
00:17:29,447 --> 00:17:41,287
Oh, jeez.

254
00:17:52,627 --> 00:17:53,827
That was close.

255
00:17:56,567 --> 00:17:58,347
Why did the traps go off?

256
00:17:58,347 --> 00:18:01,767
Hey! The trap's activated over there! Surround the hallway!

257
00:18:02,767 --> 00:18:04,247
Crap! The guards are coming!

258
00:18:05,467 --> 00:18:05,987
Halt!

259
00:18:12,887 --> 00:18:13,807
They're gone!

260
00:18:14,207 --> 00:18:15,187
That was lucky.

261
00:18:19,407 --> 00:18:19,927
Huh?

262
00:18:20,527 --> 00:18:22,747
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

263
00:18:23,347 --> 00:18:25,687
Buddy, slow down. Hold on a second.

264
00:18:25,767 --> 00:18:26,387
Kind of busy.

265
00:18:26,387 --> 00:18:29,687
Yeah, that's what it looks like, but how the heck did you get out of your cell?

266
00:18:30,147 --> 00:18:31,307
Hey, what's going on?

267
00:18:31,767 --> 00:18:34,547
I didn't get out. I came in from the outside.

268
00:18:34,967 --> 00:18:35,707
Well, bye!

269
00:18:35,827 --> 00:18:38,767
Hey, hold up! There's no way that's the truth!

270
00:18:39,007 --> 00:18:40,347
Uh-huh, it's so true.

271
00:18:40,447 --> 00:18:41,907
You don't look like a jailer.

272
00:18:41,987 --> 00:18:44,127
So who are you and why the hell are you here?

273
00:18:44,647 --> 00:18:46,787
He's not behind bars, so maybe it's true.

274
00:18:47,427 --> 00:18:49,367
You guys have some really bad attitudes.

275
00:18:50,087 --> 00:18:52,587
Wait a sec. Any of you know where I can find Ace?

276
00:18:52,587 --> 00:18:59,187
Uh, Ace? Wait, Ace? You mean him? The guy on death row?

277
00:19:00,747 --> 00:19:03,387
That's the one. I came here to bust him out of this place.

278
00:19:04,547 --> 00:19:05,927
Yeah, good luck with that.

279
00:19:06,207 --> 00:19:09,807
We don't get a lot of info down here, but I heard they just brought him in.

280
00:19:09,967 --> 00:19:13,087
If that's true and he is here, then he's got to be on level five.

281
00:19:13,207 --> 00:19:15,827
No way you're getting down there. You're screwed, pal.

282
00:19:15,827 --> 00:19:20,547
That's the floor where they hold all the prisoners with a bounty of a hundred million or more.

283
00:19:23,447 --> 00:19:24,707
Level five, huh?

284
00:19:25,027 --> 00:19:30,027
Oh, and by the way, pal, why you're here, you think you could run to the jailer's room and pick us up some keys?

285
00:19:31,467 --> 00:19:33,327
Yeah, buddy. Wouldn't be no trouble, right?

286
00:19:33,607 --> 00:19:37,507
This has got to be destiny, man. I mean, what else would bring us together like this?

287
00:19:37,667 --> 00:19:40,087
It's like you were born to set us free, right?

288
00:19:40,087 --> 00:19:44,687
What are those things?

289
00:19:46,407 --> 00:19:47,607
Stop looking forwarding!

290
00:19:47,907 --> 00:19:48,967
I don't like them!

291
00:19:49,187 --> 00:19:51,547
Run! Homie, they're gonna kill you!

292
00:20:00,927 --> 00:20:03,587
Hurry! We're taking them back! I like you!

293
00:20:03,967 --> 00:20:07,807
Right side! And left side!

294
00:20:07,807 --> 00:20:10,667
You're dying!

295
00:20:12,067 --> 00:20:13,807
How you like that, suckers?

296
00:20:13,927 --> 00:20:16,887
You can cut me all you want! I ain't the chop-chop fruit!

297
00:20:21,767 --> 00:20:23,127
Straw rats!

298
00:20:23,627 --> 00:20:25,667
What the hell are you doing here?

299
00:20:37,807 --> 00:20:41,527
Oh, buggy.

300
00:20:42,027 --> 00:20:44,967
Ah! Thanks for reminding me why I hate you!

301
00:20:45,187 --> 00:20:47,427
I see prison hasn't made you any less annoying.

302
00:20:47,867 --> 00:20:51,047
Speaking of, guess that King of the Pirates thing ain't working out too well.

303
00:20:51,127 --> 00:20:52,347
I came here on my own.

304
00:20:52,407 --> 00:20:54,887
Only dumb people like you get caught and thrown in jail.

305
00:20:54,927 --> 00:20:55,627
Say what?

306
00:20:55,767 --> 00:20:58,627
You threw yourself in jail and you're calling me the dumb one?

307
00:20:58,627 --> 00:21:01,247
You must have known I was here.

308
00:21:01,467 --> 00:21:03,447
That's the real reason you broke in, isn't it?

309
00:21:03,747 --> 00:21:05,847
To save me?

310
00:21:07,647 --> 00:21:09,487
I'm not into you, weirdo!

311
00:21:09,607 --> 00:21:12,127
Just shut up and get the hell out of my way!

312
00:21:12,487 --> 00:21:14,707
I told Hancock I'd take care of myself

313
00:21:14,707 --> 00:21:17,747
and you got all these stupid axe monkeys chasing after me!

314
00:21:18,007 --> 00:21:20,627
Oh! I see! This is all about you, is it?

315
00:21:20,707 --> 00:21:22,247
Stop touching me, you clown!

316
00:21:22,247 --> 00:21:22,747
No!

317
00:21:29,067 --> 00:21:43,507
This is supposed to be a cinch!

318
00:21:43,507 --> 00:21:46,007
I called it Buggy's peaceful escape plan!

319
00:21:46,147 --> 00:21:47,647
Does this look peaceful to you?

320
00:21:47,707 --> 00:21:49,147
Who cares?

321
00:21:52,247 --> 00:21:54,007
They're surrounding us, damn it!

322
00:21:54,127 --> 00:21:56,007
I hate this!

323
00:21:56,127 --> 00:21:58,187
Hey, shouldn't we just beat those things up?

324
00:21:58,527 --> 00:22:00,627
Easy for you to say you haven't been tortured.

325
00:22:01,027 --> 00:22:02,807
Oh, how my delicate body has suffered

326
00:22:02,807 --> 00:22:04,387
from the blows of these monsters.

327
00:22:04,767 --> 00:22:07,187
Why do you think I'm running away in the first place?

328
00:22:07,607 --> 00:22:09,687
Yeah, but I wasn't planning to lose.

329
00:22:09,847 --> 00:22:11,807
Right, clearly you thought this out.

330
00:22:11,947 --> 00:22:13,147
I'm on a mission here.

331
00:22:13,387 --> 00:22:14,787
My cover's already been blown,

332
00:22:14,887 --> 00:22:16,507
so I gotta get this done in a hurry.

333
00:22:18,647 --> 00:22:20,627
You know, that's the number one reason

334
00:22:20,627 --> 00:22:22,887
why I hate you and that redhead so much.

335
00:22:23,407 --> 00:22:24,967
Both of you are always so optimistic

336
00:22:24,967 --> 00:22:26,367
in the worst way possible.

337
00:22:30,287 --> 00:22:31,527
All right, fine.

338
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:33,467
I'll go along with your crazy plan.

339
00:22:33,847 --> 00:22:35,767
It's not like I have a choice!

340
00:22:37,787 --> 00:22:39,407
Time for my specialty!

341
00:22:41,987 --> 00:22:43,267
Causing chaos!

342
00:22:44,067 --> 00:22:45,447
Works for me!

343
00:22:50,627 --> 00:23:09,447
After forming an unlikely alliance,

344
00:23:09,727 --> 00:23:11,547
Muffy is able to race through Impel Down

345
00:23:11,547 --> 00:23:14,127
thanks to the help of Buggy's chop-chop powers.

346
00:23:14,707 --> 00:23:16,227
However, when they make their way

347
00:23:16,227 --> 00:23:18,067
to what is known as the Crimson Hell,

348
00:23:18,267 --> 00:23:19,627
they discover their descent

349
00:23:19,627 --> 00:23:21,947
will not be as swift as it foresees.

350
00:23:22,187 --> 00:23:23,607
On the next One Piece,

351
00:23:23,947 --> 00:23:25,467
Breakthrough the Crimson Hell,

352
00:23:25,927 --> 00:23:27,927
Buggy's chaos-inducing plan,

353
00:23:28,387 --> 00:23:30,147
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

